# The MCP service on Coolify (application "mcp", port 8106, domain https://mcp.callerwhale.com). The one address people paste into Claude, ChatGPT or Gemini to connect Caller Whale. It keeps no data; it asks the auth service who each access token belongs to.
# Paste into Environment Variables -> Developer View. Fill every <...>.
# MCP HTTP listening port; default 8106. Match Coolify's container port and the domain's upstream.
PORT=8106
# This service's own public address as assistants reach it (https, no trailing slash). It is the resource an assistant asks permission for; a wrong value breaks sign-in discovery.
MCP_PUBLIC_URL=https://mcp.callerwhale.com
# The auth service's public address, where assistants send the person to allow the connection. Keep it the same as AUTH_PUBLIC_URL on auth.
MCP_AUTH_PUBLIC_URL=https://auth.callerwhale.com
# The auth service's private address on the shared Docker network (http://auth:8101), used to ask who a token belongs to. Never a public address.
MCP_AUTH_URL=http://auth:8101
# Secret shared with auth (its AUTH_MCP_TOKEN), 32+ characters. Rotate both together; a mismatch refuses every connection.
MCP_AUTH_TOKEN=<32+ random characters>
